---
title: Sloppy Joes
description: Sloppy joes with beef tossed in baking soda and mashed fine with a potato masher.
tags: [sandwich]
course: main
cuisine: American
source:
  name: America's Test Kitchen
  url: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/11534-classic-sloppy-joes
servings: 4
time: 45m
---

Combine @water{1%tbsp} and @baking soda{1/2%tsp} in a #small bowl{}.

In a #large bowl{}, toss the @85 percent lean ground beef{1%lb} with the baking soda mixture and @table salt{1/2%tsp} until thoroughly combined. Set aside.

Heat the @vegetable oil{2%tsp} in a 12-inch nonstick #skillet{} over medium heat until shimmering. Add the @onion{1/2}(chopped fine) and the remaining @&baking soda{1/8%tsp} and stir to coat. Cook, stirring occasionally, until the onion is softened, ~cook{3-4%minutes}.

Add the @garlic cloves{2}(minced) and cook, stirring constantly, until fragrant, about ~cook{30%seconds}.

Stir in the @packed brown sugar{2%tsp}(plus extra for seasoning), @paprika{2%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp}, and the remaining @&table salt{1/8%tsp} and cook, stirring constantly, until the paprika is fragrant, about ~cook{1%minute}.

Add the @tomato paste{1/4%cup} and cook, stirring constantly, until the paste is rust-colored, ~cook{3-4%minutes}.

Add the beef and cook, breaking up the meat with a #wooden spoon{}, until the beef is no longer pink, about ~cook{5%minutes}. Mash the beef with a #potato masher{} until fine-textured, about ~mash{1%minute}.

Add the @ketchup{1/3%cup}, @red wine vinegar{1%tbsp}(plus extra for seasoning), and @Worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp} and stir to combine, scraping up any browned bits.

Combine the @cornstarch{1/2%tsp} and the remaining @&water{1%tbsp} in a #&small bowl{}, then pour the cornstarch mixture over the beef and stir to incorporate. Cook, stirring constantly, until the sauce thickens and coats the beef, about ~cook{1%minute}.

Season with salt, extra sugar, and extra vinegar to taste. Spoon the beef mixture onto the @hamburger buns{4} and serve.
